- Further, you can modify your code as follows:
```
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    char *s = "HI!";
    printf("%c\n", *s);
    printf("%c\n", *(s + 1));
    printf("%c\n", *(s + 2));
}
```Notice that the first character at the location of `s` is printed. Then, the character at the location `s + 1` is printed, and so on.

